Z||000000||2xsess||01-28-2001||11:45 PM||||WEll, I did a search on O2 sensor and even looked in the Archives and didn't find the answer.<P>I changed the O2 sensor and the fuel filter today. Then I started it up and the idle jumped around between 1100RPMS and 500RPMS. I then drove it about 40miles at 55mph. When I got to where I was going it idled ok, no jumping around. then I let it sit for about an hour. Started it up and it did the same thing.<BR> <BR>My question is , is this normal right after changing the sensor? Shouldn't the ECM have reset after the driving I did?<P>TIA<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2xsess.gif">    <BR> <A HREF="http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html" TARGET=_blank>http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html</A>||||reg||1
